<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 May, from 1152 to 1980.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1152">1152 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">874 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry of Anjou marries Eleanor of Aquitaine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry of Anjou, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a>, married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a> after the annulment of her marriage to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france">Louis VII of France</a>. She brought Aquitaine into the Angevin Empire, and Henry became king two years later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1291">1291 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">735 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mamluks capture Acre, the last great crusader city</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> al-Ashraf Khalil's army stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> after a six-week siege. The remaining crusader towns on the coast were abandoned within months, ending the crusader states in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1302">1302 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">724 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Flemish townsmen massacre the French garrison in Bruges</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before dawn, Flemish townsmen led by Pieter de Coninck and Jan Breydel massacred the French garrison installed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a>. The revolt led to the Flemish victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-golden-spurs">Battle of the Golden Spurs</a> in July.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matins-of-bruges">Matins of Bruges</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1388">1388 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">638 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ming general Lan Yu routs the Northern Yuan at Buyur Lake</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Ming army under Lan Yu surprised the camp of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-yuan">Northern Yuan</a> khan Toghus Temür near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-buir">Lake Buir</a>, capturing tens of thousands of people. The khan escaped but was soon killed by a rival, and Northern Yuan authority collapsed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-buyur-lake">Battle of Buyur Lake</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-yuan">Northern Yuan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1804">1804 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French Senate proclaims Napoleon Emperor of the French</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A decree of the Senate made First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> hereditary emperor. He crowned himself in Notre-Dame in December, in the presence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii">Pope Pius VII</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1860">1860 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">166 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Republicans nominate Abraham Lincoln for president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Chicago convention Lincoln overtook the favourite, William Seward, on the third ballot. His election in November prompted Southern states to secede.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Plessy v. Ferguson upholds 'separate but equal'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Supreme Court ruled that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/racial-segregation">racial segregation</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> railways did not violate the Constitution. The decision underpinned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jim-crow-laws">Jim Crow laws</a> until Brown v. Board of Education in 1954.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1980">1980 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">46 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mount St Helens erupts in Washington State</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake triggered a vast landslide and lateral blast that tore away the mountain's north face. Fifty-seven people died in the deadliest eruption in US history.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 May <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ruder-boskovic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ruder-boskovic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ruđer Bošković</span><span class="tp">1711–1787</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eurico-gaspar-dutra"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eurico-gaspar-dutra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eurico Gaspar Dutra</span><span class="tp">1883–1974</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-gropius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-gropius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Gropius</span><span class="tp">1883–1969</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/augusto-cesar-sandino"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/augusto-cesar-sandino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Augusto César Sandino</span><span class="tp">1895–1934</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-ii-of-opole"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wladyslaw-ii-of-opole.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Władysław II of Opole</span><span class="tp">c. 1332–1401</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-germany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rupert-of-germany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rupert of Germany</span><span class="tp">1352–1410</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jacques-marquette"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jacques-marquette.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jacques Marquette</span><span class="tp">1637–1675</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tupac-amaru-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tupac-amaru-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Túpac Amaru II</span><span class="tp">1738–1781</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dobrica-cosic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dobrica-cosic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dobrica Ćosić</span><span class="tp">1921–2014</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
